    "total_efficiency_score": 721.7,
    "narrative": "Our top-tier offensive output today is anchored by **Corbin Carroll** (80.77) and **Josh Naylor** (72.66), both of whom benefit significantly from favorable matchups against Quintana and Lugo, respectively. **Corbin Carroll** is in a prime spot to exploit a generous 5.24 xERA matchup, with his efficiency bolstered by an elite 19% SP Skill projection bonus and a favorable batting order position. Meanwhile, **Josh Naylor** provides a high-floor, high-ceiling play in the heart of the order, leveraging a strong park factor and a 10% SP skill edge to remain a must-start in all formats. **James Wood** (71.88) also rounds out our elite tier; despite facing a lefty, his xwOBA of .379 and premium leadoff spot provide the necessary volume and efficiency to justify the start, even against the moderate challenge of P\u00e9rez.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Kyle Karros** (46.44), who fell just shy of the threshold to displace our lower-performing starters. While his raw base projections were competitive, the combination of a bottom-third batting order and a neutral matchup against Nelson pushed him out of the starting nine. We also monitored **Jose Caballero** (44.46) closely; although his profile typically gains value in our stolen base-heavy build, a unfavorable wind forecast and a poor platoon split against Rasmussen suppressed his efficiency score, making him a high-risk gamble we preferred to avoid in favor of our projected starters like **Zach McKinstry**, who is seeing a massive 16% park boost today.\n\nRegarding risks, managers should keep a close eye on **Brice Turang** (47.97). While he is slotted into the two-hole, his efficiency is weighed down by an aggressive 17% penalty for facing the elite arm of Yamamoto. Furthermore, the base scoring for **Dalton Rushing** (51.36) remains marginal due to his seventh-spot position in the order and the risk posed by Sproat\u2019s ability to control the running game, which slightly dilutes his offensive utility. We are proceeding with the current lineup, keeping **Carson Williams** and **Henry Bolte** on standby should any late-scratch lineup announcements shift our strategy.",
